{"Cache key uses hash() which is non-deterministic across processes - Python's built-in hash() is randomized per process via PYTHONHASHSEED, breaking cross-process cache sharing and making invalidate_upsampling_cache() unable to invalidate entries set by other processes": 0.9785107374191284, "_is_error_focused_query matches negated queries like !event.type:error - the substring check \"event.type:error\" in query will incorrectly match negated queries, causing upsampling to be applied to queries that explicitly exclude error events": 0.9786974787712097, "invalidate_upsampling_cache is dead code - the function is defined but never called anywhere in the codebase, should either be wired into option-change signal/hook or removed": 0.890271008014679}